From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:47:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: msm8998: vote the bus for a 4k60 decode load

The msm8998 decoder bandwidth table stopped at the 4k30 row, so a
2160p60 session (1944000 macroblocks/s) landed on that row and voted
2.365 GB/s for twice the traffic. Add a 4k60 row at twice the 4k30
figures, still under the 4946000 kBps ceiling the vendor's msm8998
video node declares for this path.

Measured on a Pixel 2 XL: the venus VP9 decoder already reaches 82 fps
at 3840x2160 through GStreamer into a sink that accepts video metadata,
and 69 fps through ffmpeg, on the old vote; this row is the honest vote
for that load, not the fix for a throughput problem.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 4712652d1aca..1c8aacc5283a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -909,6 +909,7 @@ static const struct reg_val msm8998_reg_preset[] = {
  * calibrating against the vendor's dynamic governor before 4k60 is trusted.
  */
 static const struct bw_tbl msm8998_bw_table_dec[] = {
+	{ 1944000,  4730000, 0, 3784000, 0 },	/* 4k UHD @ 60: 2x the 4k30 row, under the vendor's 4946000 kBps ceiling */
 	{  979200,  2365000, 0, 1892000, 0 },	/* 4k UHD @ 30 */
 	{  864000,  1978000, 0, 1554000, 0 },	/* 720p @ 240 */
 	{  489600,  1133000, 0,  895000, 0 },	/* 1080p @ 60 */
